 "notes": "CardDemo's fraud-report service (COPAUS2C), LINKed by COPAUS1C in its task (transaction CPVD, app/app-authorization-ims-db2-mq/csd/CRDDEMO2.csd) (the pending-authorization detail screen, held by its IMS DL/I calls) with DFHCOMMAREA: the account and customer ids, the pending authorization (COPY CIPAUDTY, the IMS segment) and the fraud action. It FORMATTIMEs the task's ASKTIME into PA-FRAUD-RPT-DATE, builds AUTH_TS from the authorization's original date and its inverted time key, and INSERTs the authorization into CARDDEMO.AUTHFRDS (FRAUD_RPT_DATE = CURRENT DATE); a duplicate key (-803) UPDATEs AUTH_FRAUD / FRAUD_RPT_DATE of the row instead; any other SQLCODE is 'F' with the SQLCODE / SQLSTATE in the message. The result is the COMMAREA it leaves (\"linked\": true) and the table. Db2 is the DDL's table and unique index with seed.sql's one reported row. FRAUD_RPT_DATE is Db2's CURRENT DATE on both sides (the same container, the same day; a run across midnight would differ). Not exercised: COPAUS1C itself (IMS). Derived from the AWS Mainframe Modernization CardDemo application (Apache-2.0): LICENSE here is the corpus's own, NOTICE names the source and what was derived."
